[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Scandinavian Defense"]
[Variation "Scandinavian Defense: Gubinsky-Melts Defense"]
[ECO "B01"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "centre-control,quick-development"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3...Qd6"]
[Start "1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3"]

3... Qd6 4. d4 { Takes the centre. Black's queen on d6 can later be hit by Bf4 or Nb5. } 4... Nf6 ( 4... c6 5. Nf3 Nf6 6. h3 { Stops ...Bg4 before White has developed the bishops. } ) 5. Nf3 a6 6. Bd3 { Develops toward the kingside and clears the first rank for castling. } 6... g6 ( 6... Nc6 7. O-O ) ( 6... Bg4 7. h3 { Asks the bishop what it wants: trade on f3 or retreat. } 7... Bxf3 8. Qxf3 ) 7. O-O { Castles early so the king is safe before the centre opens. } 7... Bg7 8. Re1 { Puts the rook on the e-file, where the centre will open, and makes room for Bf4 to hit the queen. Plan: Bf4, Qd2, and a kingside attack if Black castles there. } *
